Project Description
This diabetes prediction model uses machine learning algorithms to predict whether a patient has diabetes based on certain health parameters. The model is enhanced with Gemini LLM to provide natural language explanations and feedback about the predictions. The user interface is created with Streamlit, allowing users to input data and view results interactively. Docker is used for containerization, making it easy to deploy the app across multiple platforms.

Installation Guide
Follow these steps to set up and run the project on your local machine:

Navigate to Project Folder:
cd diabetes-predictor

Create and Activate Virtual Environment (optional but recommended):
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate (for Linux/macOS)
venv\Scripts\activate (for Windows)

Install Dependencies:
Run the following command to install all required dependencies:
pip install -r requirements.txt

Usage
After setting up the project, follow these steps to run the application:

Run the Streamlit app:
streamlit run app.py

Open your browser and navigate to the displayed URL (usually http://localhost:8501) to interact with the UI.

Input the necessary health parameters to get diabetes predictions, and receive a natural language explanation of the result, thanks to Gemini LLM.

Dependencies
The project requires the following Python libraries:

Python 3.x

Streamlit: For building the UI (pip install streamlit)

Scikit-learn: For machine learning model implementation (pip install scikit-learn)

Pandas: For data handling (pip install pandas)

NumPy: For numerical operations (pip install numpy)

Gemini: For LLM integration (pip install gemini or your preferred method for LLM integration)

Matplotlib/Seaborn (Optional, for visualizations)

Additionally, Docker is used for containerization.

